# --- committed on purpose -----------------------------------------------------
#
# data/corpus/documents.jsonl  The fetched corpus IS committed, even though `ragmed
#   ingest` can rebuild it. PubMed is a moving target: re-running ingestion months
#   later returns a different set of papers, which changes the chunk ids, which
#   silently invalidates every gold label in the golden set. Committing the corpus is
#   what makes the evaluation reproducible by anyone who clones this.
#
# data/golden/  The golden set - the contract every eval number is measured against.
#
# runs/  The measured results behind the README's tables. Small, and they are the
#   evidence for the claims.

# --- not committed ------------------------------------------------------------
# Indexes are deterministic given the corpus + config fingerprint, so rebuilding
# them is exact rather than approximate. `ragmed index` regenerates in ~1 minute.
data/index/
data/cache/
data/raw/
*.npy
*.npz
*.faiss

# Raw console dumps: tqdm progress bars and ANSI noise, superseded by the JSON
# artifacts in runs/<label>/ that carry the same numbers in a readable form.
runs/*.txt

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.DS_Store
